{"name":"Costa Rican Palm","hex":"#c44041","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"costa","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of rib.","A riblike part of a plant or animal, such as a midrib of a leaf or a thickened vein or the margin of an insect wing.\n The vein forming the leading edge of most insect wings."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/costa"},{"term":"palm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various evergreen trees from the family Palmae or Arecaceae, which are mainly found in the tropics.","A branch or leaf of the palm, anciently borne or worn as a symbol of victory or rejoicing."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The inner and somewhat concave part of the human hand or other primate hand that extends from the wrist to the bases of the fingers.","The corresponding part of the forefoot of a nonprimate mammal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/palm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Costa Rica","blocks":[{"text":"Costa Rica, officially the Republic of Costa Rica, is a country in Central America. It borders Nicaragua to the north, the Caribbean Sea to the northeast, Panama to the southeast, and the Pacific Ocean to the southwest, sharing a maritime border with Ecuador to the south of Cocos Island. It has a population of around five million in a land area of nearly 51,180 km2 (19,760 sq mi); the capital and largest city is San José, home to around 350,000 residents and two million people in the surrounding metropolitan area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Flag_of_Costa_Rica.svg/330px-Flag_of_Costa_Rica.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Costa_Rica"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Stone_spheres_of_Costa_Rica._Museo_Nacional.jpg/500px-Stone_spheres_of_Costa_Rica._Museo_Nacional.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parse